            "id": "a-1792444735557",
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "To give a definitive yes or no, I need your exact laptop model, but most modern laptops with 16 GB of RAM support up to 32 GB or 64 GB unless the RAM is soldered.\n\nYou can check your system's hardware limit directly in Command Prompt by running:\n\n```cmd\nwmic memphysical get maxcapacity, memorydevices\n```\n\nDivide the `MaxCapacity` output (given in kilobytes) by `1048576` to get the maximum supported gigabytes. If `MemoryDevices` shows 2, your motherboard has two slots.\n\n**Key terms:**\n* **SODIMM:** Small Outline Dual In-line Memory Module, the standard removable RAM stick format for laptops.\n* **Soldered RAM:** Memory chips permanently welded onto the motherboard that cannot be replaced or upgraded.",
            "timestamp": "10:18:55 PM",
            "isStreaming": false
          },
          {
            "id": "u-1792444829223",
            "role": "user",
            "content": "check it yourself",
            "timestamp": "10:20:29 PM"
